Debian GNU/Linux installer 13 (trixie), installer build 20250803+deb13u7:
https://www.debian.org/devel/debian-installer/
https://deb.debian.org/debian/dists/trixie/main/installer-amd64/20250803+deb13u7/images/
The image is assembled freshly from the official kernel and netboot initrd.
The installer is an aggregation of separately licensed components. The builder
preserves its original package status and generates installer-components.json
with package/source versions, versioned source URLs, and per-source copyright
URLs. A binary package's source package may have a different name. The Debian
source package's debian/copyright file states that component's license terms.

Linux 6.12.107+deb13-amd64, Debian source package linux 6.12.107-1:
https://sources.debian.org/src/linux/6.12.107-1/
https://sources.debian.org/src/linux/6.12.107-1/debian/copyright/
Linux is primarily GPL-2.0-only with additional component-specific terms and
exceptions documented in the corresponding source, including LICENSES/.
Exact-kernel storage udebs are verified against official Packages SHA256 entries
before only lib/modules/6.12.107+deb13-amd64 is merged into the usrmerged initrd.

GNU GRUB (Debian source grub2), same-version tools and BIOS/x64 EFI/IA32 EFI
modules, with package copyrights included under licenses/packages/:
https://www.gnu.org/software/grub/
https://sources.debian.org/src/grub2/
GRUB is primarily GPL-3.0-or-later; its source/package copyright files cover
exceptions and individual files. Unsigned loaders do not support Secure Boot.

Additional embedded programs: curl/libcurl, OpenSSH ssh-keygen, GNU coreutils od,
their loader/shared-library dependency closure, and ca-certificates trust roots.
Their actual installed Debian package/source versions and source URLs are
recorded in component-packages.json. Package copyright files are copied under
licenses/packages/PACKAGE/copyright; full common license texts are included under
licenses/common-licenses/. The same notices appear in the initrd under
/usr/share/doc/cxt-debian13-public/ and on both raw and ISO boot volumes.
Examples (not an exhaustive license list): curl uses the curl license, OpenSSH
uses BSD-style terms, coreutils uses GPL-3.0-or-later, glibc uses LGPL terms with
component exceptions, and the trust-root bundle has its own notices.

Corresponding source and copyright resources:
https://sources.debian.org/ (browse exact source package/version from manifests)
https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/ (Debian .dsc and orig/debian source archives)
https://snapshot.debian.org/ (archived exact versions if removed from mirrors)
https://www.debian.org/legal/licenses/
On a Debian system with matching deb-src entries, use:
    apt-get source 'SOURCE_PACKAGE=SOURCE_VERSION'
Use source package names/versions from the generated manifests, not an assumed
binary package name. Keep corresponding source available with binary releases
as required by the respective component licenses; do not substitute this notice
for those obligations. The new overlay and builder corresponding source is this
public repository. The raw/ISO are network installers, not installed OS backups.

Input integrity: inputs.json pins the official cached files. Their original
acquisition checked SHA256SUMS or Packages through verified HTTPS; detached
Debian signatures were not independently checked at that acquisition step.
Normal Debian installer/APT archive signature verification remains enabled.
